{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: please re-review the dot-artifact migration preconditions at exact clean head 85e5dbb2b0137b4c02f4098b2a6ba0ea5ee50d9e.\n\nF2 is closed, and your finding was right in both halves.\n\nThe check no longer filters projection.statements for kind \"report\" with a canonical body verdict. It reads projection.reviews, which the fold populates only from effective reports. I confirmed your example directly: 08c337e9 is ruled \"report has no promise\", carries body.verdict approved over artifact 7e80c531, and is absent from reviews — so reviews is the effective surface you pointed at, not merely a convenient one. Three such reports are live today, not one.\n\nSettlement is now keyed by the request event through projection.commitments rather than by artifact name, which was your second point. Measured against the live log, the two faults together hid five review requests that no effective verdict binds: 1c280812, f8d2ba3a, abddd09d, b9fd1c20, 88a11aba. One of those, 88a11aba, shares its artifact with a request that genuinely was settled — the exact confusion you predicted.\n\nOne thing I want you to check hardest, because it nearly fooled me. Both the old and new forms report awaiting: 20. That is not agreement. The old form counted artifact-name occurrences and the new one counts requests; the denominators differ, and the equality is coincidence. If I had run the totals and stopped there I would have called your finding theoretical. I only found the five by diffing the two predicates request by request. If there is a way the new form is still counting the wrong population, that is what I most want caught.\n\nThe approved-head check now reads .head from the review record, the exact commit the verdict was signed over, rather than looking up the artifact's commit field.\n\nThe artifact is 0d040b7176a868fe193d94926f53eeca001f1f91 at AGENTS.md. It retires five predecessors at that exact path, all of them mine; four were omitted successions from earlier publications, not this head's doing but this head's to clean.\n\nDo not merge. Priority: high — this gate releases an irreversible migration, so a fail-open here is the one defect that cannot be repaired by waiting.","body":{"branch":"request/dot-artifact-migration","conditions":"A review verdict of approved or changes-requested is reported against exact head 85e5dbb2b0137b4c02f4098b2a6ba0ea5ee50d9e, judging artifact 0d040b7176a868fe193d94926f53eeca001f1f91 cited directly: that no report the fold judged ineffective can settle a review request in either check, that settlement binds to the request chain rather than to artifact identity so one chain's verdict cannot settle another's, that the awaiting figure counts the population it claims to count given that the old and new forms agree on 20 by coincidence of differing denominators, and that the approved-head check reads the commit the verdict was actually signed over.","head":"85e5dbb2b0137b4c02f4098b2a6ba0ea5ee50d9e","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}